---
description: Execution safety for exchange-facing code
globs: execution/**
---
- Default broker is PaperBroker. LiveBroker instantiation must assert LIVE_TRADING=1 and a signed capital_allocation.yaml (`execution.gate.assert_live_allowed`).
- Every order has: client_order_id (idempotent), max_slippage_bps, time_in_force, kill-after. These are required fields on `execution.broker.Order`; do not make them optional.
- Reconcile positions with exchange every 60s; on mismatch > 1% → halt + alert.
- Use post-only/maker where latency permits; model taker cost otherwise.
- Rate-limit aware; exponential backoff; never retry a filled-ambiguous order blindly.
- Exchange outages / 5xx for > 2 min → cancel all open orders, go flat if in directional risk.
- No order-placement capability is ever exposed through MCP. Orders go through code, behind the LIVE gate.
- Every change here ships with tests and a fill-quality report (realised vs modelled cost).
